    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This NCEI Accession includes surface underway chemical, physical and meteorological measurements during the R/V Xue Long CHINARE2016 Expedition (EXPOCODE 76XL20160724) in the Bering Sea, Chukchi Sea and Arctic Ocean from 2016-07-24 to 2016-09-04. These data include measurements of Mole fraction of CO2 in the equilibrator headspace (dry) at equilibrator temperature, in parts per million, mole fraction of CO2 measured in dry outside air, barometric pressure in the equilibrator headspace, barometric pressure, corrected to sea level, water temperature in equilibrator, sea surface temperature, sea surface salinity, fugacity of CO2 in sea water at SST and 100% humidity, and difference between sea water fCO2 and interpolated air fCO2. The instruments used to collect these data include carbon dioxide (CO2) gas analyzer and shower head chamber equilibrator for autonomous carbon dioxide (CO2) measurement.",
